@startuml ordered-cost-theory-layers
' Ordered Residual Calculus and its lazy product specialization.
skinparam backgroundColor #FFFFFF
skinparam shadowing false
skinparam defaultFontName "DejaVu Sans"
skinparam rectangle {
  BorderColor #37474F
  FontColor #102027
  RoundCorner 12
}
skinparam ArrowColor #37474F
skinparam ArrowThickness 2

title Ordered Residual Calculus — semantics, realization, and execution

rectangle "Measure specification\nquery, domain, output observation" as Measure #E3F2FD
rectangle "Residual behavior\nexists for every measure" as Residual #BBDEFB
rectangle "Ordered cost transformations\nminimum + composition" as Algebra #FFE0B2
rectangle "Certified executable realization\nfinite states, registers, or history" as Realization #D1C4E9
rectangle "Executable simulation preorder\nproved frontier normalization" as Simulation #D1C4E9
rectangle "Observed-transition machine\nexact interning + compact StateId" as Machine #B2EBF2
rectangle "Reachable synchronized product\ndictionary cursor × StateId" as Product #C8E6C9
rectangle "Abstract interval product\ncandidate superset" as Abstract #FFF9C4
rectangle "Exact original verification\nauthoritative membership and cost" as Verify #F8BBD0
rectangle "Metric-qualified instance\ndomain/quotient axioms" as Metric #DCEDC8

Measure --> Residual : input derivatives
Measure --> Metric : separate geometric proof
Residual --> Realization : effective representation proof
Algebra --> Realization : recurrence instances
Realization --> Simulation : minimum-frontier specialization
Simulation --> Machine : canonical live state
Machine --> Product : edge-demanded transition
Product --> Verify : exact result contract
Product --> Abstract : interval labels
Abstract --> Verify : verify every collision member

note right of Product #E8F5E9
  Product names the operational construction.
  Intersection names the accepted language
  when both components are exact acceptors.
end note

note bottom of Realization #E3F2FD
  Exact morphisms compose realizations.
  Lower simulations compose bounds.
  Backward budgets derive safe pruning.
  Bounded registers need separate bit bounds.
end note

note bottom of Metric #FFF9C4
  Metricity does not imply finite state.
  Rounded outputs need a numerical proof
  before triangle-based pruning applies.
end note
@enduml
